# Database Rules for AvidX repos

## CRITICAL
- NEVER run `prisma db push` in any form, especially with `--accept-data-loss`. This command is BANNED across all AvidX repos.
- For schema changes, ALWAYS use `prisma migrate dev --name <descriptive_name>`. This generates a named migration file under `prisma/migrations/` for review.
- For production, use `prisma migrate deploy` only.

## Why this matters
The database is SHARED across AvidX products (Watch Me, Mail Zero, Planfinity, Memodee, Signal). Other products' tables (signal_*, mail_zero_*, etc.) appear as "drift" to this product's Prisma schema but MUST NOT be deleted.

## If you see drift
- If `prisma migrate dev` generates a migration containing DROP TABLE for anything outside this product's namespace, STOP and ask the user.
- If Prisma reports drift you don't recognize, STOP and ask the user.
- Treat anything you didn't add yourself as untouchable.

## Reference
See AVIDX-259 in Linear for full policy.